  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Sources of record</h6>
        <p>Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, National Statistics Office: National Accounts Statistics (GVA by industry and sub-industry, 2011-12 and 2022-23 bases), the trial Index of Services Production (base 2024-25), the Periodic Labour Force Survey and the Annual Survey of Unincorporated Sector Enterprises, all through the eSankhyiki API. Reserve Bank of India: monthly trade in services, the balance of payments by category and purpose code, and the long annual invisibles table, from its Database on Indian Economy through our local, read-only mirror. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={V["prov-vintage"]}></b>; trade vintage <b id="prov-trade-v" set:html={V["prov-trade-v"]}></b>.</p>
        <p>Checked by hand against the agencies' own releases: MoSPI's first ISP release (14 July 2026: retail trade 130.5 for 2025-26, 137.50 for April 2026) and its 29 July release (retail trade up 13.3% in May 2026); the RBI's balance-of-payments press release of 27 June 2025 (net services US$ 53.3 billion in January to March 2025, US$ 42.7 billion a year earlier); and its 30 June 2026 release on monthly services trade (May 2026 receipts US$ 33,355 million, payments US$ 17,637 million).</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Shares of GVA are computed from published current-price levels; real growth from constant-price levels, never taken from rounded published rates. The services total is the sum of the published service groups. ISP growth is computed from the index and checked against MoSPI's rates. RBI values are stored once each (DBIE repeats every value once per display unit), and for each period the most mature version is used. PLFS and ASUSE values are published shares, counts and rupee figures, shown as published.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Never joined: the 2011-12 and 2022-23 national accounts bases; the RBI's older invisibles categories and BPM6; PLFS agriculture-year reports, the original design's calendar-year estimates (2023, 2024) and the revamped design's (2025 on: MoSPI redesigned the survey from January 2025); ASUSE financial-year rounds and the 2025 calendar-year round. On the 2011-12 base, MoSPI serves the three combined service groups only as advance and provisional estimates while their parts carry later revisions; the services total uses the parts where they exist. The RBI's 1985-86 services row does not add up as published (a five-million-dollar gap) and is kept as published.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026. Revised with each national accounts, ISP, RBI and survey release. The RBI's DBIE copy of the monthly services data lags its press releases; we follow DBIE.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <span>Measure of India, services</span>
      <span>Vintage <span id="prov-vintage2" set:html={V["prov-vintage2"]}></span></span>
      <span>Set in Newsreader and Libre Franklin</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

